The M3 change to the web workflow, not applied from the session that wrote
it (it could not push workflow files). Apply it with
`git apply web/docs/runbooks/ci-pending.patch` from the repository root and
delete this file in the same commit.

It adds a `conformance` job: replica-proto's whole suite over HTTP against the
server on a temp SQLite file (`web/packages/server/test/conformance/`, plan
01 A1), the batched convergence configuration included, and the check that
every pattern of the server's mutation set matches its code once and names
tests that exist (`npm run mutate -- --check`, seconds). The server's `npm
test` leaves the conformance directory out because it takes about 30
minutes on 4 cores, so the `test` job does not run it.

diff --git a/.github/workflows/web.yml b/.github/workflows/web.yml
--- a/.github/workflows/web.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/web.yml
@@ -46,6 +46,24 @@ jobs:
       - run: npm ci
       - run: npm test

+  # replica-proto's suite over HTTP against the SQLite server (plan 01 A1,
+  # M3). About 30 minutes, most of it the 200 convergence sequences; the
+  # server's `npm test` leaves it out.
+  conformance:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    timeout-minutes: 60
+    steps:
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
+        with:
+          node-version: 22
+          cache: npm
+          cache-dependency-path: web/package-lock.json
+      - run: npm ci
+      # the mutation set's patterns and expected tests (`test/mutations/`)
+      - run: npm run mutate --workspace @session/server -- --check
+      - run: npm test --workspace @session/server -- 'test/conformance/**'
+
   # The Playwright suite (`web/docs/12-testing-linting-ci.md` §3.6): one real
   # server with fixture providers, a temp data directory and the test-only
   # sign-in route, serving a client build through its own static middleware.
